# Google Drive integration
#
# Both values below are inlined into the shipped JS bundle by Vite
# (that's what the `VITE_` prefix opts into). They are NOT secrets —
# do not put server-side credentials behind the `VITE_` prefix.
#
# Create credentials at https://console.cloud.google.com/ following
# docs/plans/google-drive-integration.md §4 (restrict the API key to
# HTTP referrers `annot.work` + `localhost:3000` so a scraped copy is
# useless off-origin).
#
# For local dev, copy this file to `.env.local` in this directory.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY=your-api-key

# GitHub integration (individual-user storage backend)
#
# No env var is required. Auth is by personal access token pasted
# into the app — neither an OAuth App client ID nor a backend proxy
# is needed on the OSS side.
#
# See `docs/plans/github-integration.md` §1 for why: GitHub's
# OAuth Web Flow and Device Flow both require a backend to complete
# the token exchange (CORS blocks the relevant endpoints from the
# browser), and running such a backend would break the "static PWA,
# no server" property of the OSS build. A proper one-click OAuth
# UX will land on the commercial `annot-cloud` side.
